      "message": "Hi Minchan.\nI\u0027m not sure why in the following sequence:\n```\n\tptl \u003d pte_lockptr(vmf-\u003evma-\u003evm_mm, vmf-\u003epmd);\n\tpmdval \u003d READ_ONCE(*vmf-\u003epmd);\n```\npte_lockptr would read vmf-\u003epmd as 0 and READ_ONCE(*vmf-\u003epmd) would read it as non-0 (I think that\u0027s what you mean by \"no gaurantee it will see uptodate value\"). IIUC they should read either:\n1. Both non-zero (both didn\u0027t see the update)\n2. Both 0 (both saw the update)\n3. pte_lockptr reads non-zero, READ_ONCE(*vmf-\u003epmd) sees zero (update happened in between of these two statements).\n\nMaybe I\u0027m missing some memory barrier? I guess the code like this would be more robust:\n```\n\tpmdval \u003d READ_ONCE(*vmf-\u003epmd);\n\tptl \u003d pte_lockptr(vmf-\u003evma-\u003evm_mm, \u0026pmdval);\n\tif (!pmd_same(pmdval, vmf-\u003eorig_pmd))\n```\nWDYT?",
